{"ts": "2026-10-29T07:11:23.070966Z", "run_id": "r-20261029T0711Z-dbf6", "unit": "openspec:add-api-pep", "seq": 8, "type": "task.started", "task": "1.1", "title": "1.1 Write `src/api/route.test.ts` first (scenarios \"A public route registers\", \"Unwired kinds refuse\", \"A non-public route needs a known action\", \"Bad definitions\" and \"Duplicates and listeners\"; the verifier map is global, so the file registers `bearer` once and never `hmac`), then implement `defineRoute`, `registerAuthVerifier`, `RouteDefinitionError` and `listDefinedRoutes` in `src/api/route.ts`, with the Fastify augmentation in `src/api/types.ts`, implementing requirement \"A route declares a wired authentication kind and a known policy action\". `defineRoute` checks in this order and the first failure throws: (1) shape, `ROUTE_DEF_INVALID` with `details.reason` `method`, `url` (`^/[\\x21-\\x7e]*$`, no `?` or `#`), `schema` (a plain object), `errors` (unique `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}$`), `handler`, `auth` (unknown kind; `bearer.audience` 1 to 200 characters; `hmacKind` `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$`; a public `reason` outside the four), `public_options` (a public route with `action`, `resource` or `listFilter`), `resource_without_action`, `list_filter` (`kind` not `sql` or `item`, or its `predicate` or `canRead` not a function); (2) `ROUTE_LISTENER_MISMATCH` with `details.listener`: the internal listener takes only `service_token`, the public one refuses it; (3) `ROUTE_ACTION_MISSING`, then `ROUTE_ACTION_UNKNOWN` unless `Object.hasOwn(ACTIONS, action)`; (4) `ROUTE_AUTH_UNWIRED` with `details.kind`: `session` is always wired, any other non-public kind needs a registered verifier; (5) `ROUTE_DUPLICATE` with `details.route` `<METHOD> <url>`. Then `server.route(...)` with `exposeHeadRoute: false` for non-public kinds. `registerAuthVerifier` stores into one module-global map and throws `ROUTE_DUPLICATE` (`details.kind`) for `session` and for a kind already registered; an internal `verifierFor(kind)` reads it. State lives in the decorator `ursitoareRoutes` (`listener`, `defined`, `observed`), created on a bare instance with listener `public`. `listDefinedRoutes` returns the defined routes in registration order, and `[]` for a server without `ursitoareRoutes`; a route's `errors` is its declared codes plus the implied ones (non-public: `UNAUTHENTICATED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `AUTHZ_UNAVAILABLE`; `session` and not GET: `CSRF_INVALID`; `resource` set: `NOT_FOUND`), sorted and unique. Each task exports its symbols from `src/api/index.ts`. This task adds no hook: authentication arrives in 3.1"}
